.\" karvi-job(1): the manual page of karvi's job word. Written by hand except
.\" the regions between the markers, which tools/mangen rewrites from the
.\" word's help text (make generate).
.TH KARVI-JOB 1 "" "karvi"
.\" Paths and options are not hyphenated, and lines are not stretched.
.nh
.ds AD l
.ad l
.SH NAME
karvi\-job \- follow or cancel one accepted job by its ID
.SH SYNOPSIS
.\" BEGIN GENERATED SYNOPSIS: tools/mangen from internal/cli; edit there
\fBkarvi\fR \fBjob follow\fR JOB\-ID [\-\-format text|jsonl|json] [\-\-echo] [\-\-border | \-\-noborder]
.br
\fBkarvi\fR \fBjob cancel\fR JOB\-ID [\-\-reason TEXT] [\-\-follow] [\-\-format text|json]
.\" END GENERATED SYNOPSIS
.SH DESCRIPTION
.\" BEGIN GENERATED DESCRIPTION: tools/mangen from internal/cli; edit there
.PP
job operates on one accepted job, named by the job ID of its receipt (the
ID a detached run prints and karvi watch shows). No job verb launches a daemon.
.PP
follow renders the job's records from its beginning as the foreground run
would have, live until the job ends or at once for a job that has ended,
ends as the run's display ends (the footer, and a collection's line), and
exits with the job's own exit.
\-\-format, \-\-echo, \-\-border, and \-\-noborder mean what they mean for run.
Ctrl\-C stops only the follow; the job continues.
.PP
cancel stops the job and leaves every other job running; the daemon answers
at once and the job's unfinished work is recorded cancelled (exit 113).
\-\-reason TEXT is recorded with the request. \-\-follow waits for the job's end
and exits with the job's own exit. A job that already ended is reported with
its outcome; an unknown job ID is job_unknown. \-\-help shows this text.
.\" END GENERATED DESCRIPTION
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
.B karvi job follow 261003\-143005\-00
Render a detached job from its beginning; it exits with the job's exit.
.TP
.B karvi job follow 261003\-143005\-00 \-\-format jsonl
The job's records and its summary, one JSON document per line.
.TP
.B karvi job cancel 261003\-143005\-00 \-\-reason "wrong change window" \-\-follow
Stop it, record why, and wait for its end (exit 113).
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR karvi (1),
.BR karvi\-run (1),
.BR karvi\-watch (1)
